From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 17:28:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Skip slot-assignment recompute when nothing could have
 changed

Review follow-up: assignedNodesOf/assignedSlotOf flush assignments on
every call for freshness, which made a slotchange scan over S slots
cost S full recomputes across all shadow trees. A dirty flag set by
the mutations that can reshape assignment (child-list changes, slot/
name attribute writes, attach_shadow) lets the flush no-op between
changes - the first query after a mutation recomputes, the rest are
free, and every steady-state resolve() skips the walk entirely.
Starts true so the first flush always runs.
---
 src/document.rs | 9 ++++++++-
 src/mutator.rs  | 9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

